  "final_text": "I generated `input_eta_W1.700_Q2_1.000_vcut-0.1.dat` for the eta configuration with your requested point (W=1.7, Q\u00b2=1.0, cos\u03b8*=0, \u03c6*=90\u00b0) and vcut=-0.1, along with `outcome.json`.\n\nOne important caveat, flagged in `outcome.json`: I checked `eta/exclurad.F` and the negative-vcut behavior is not actually implemented. The only check on `cutv` is `if(cutv.gt.1d-12)vmax=min(vmax,cutv)` \u2014 so any vcut \u2264 0 (including -0.1) simply fails that condition and no inelasticity cut is applied at all. The README/examples describe negative vcut as \"a cut on v directly,\" but that logic doesn't exist in the source (I checked both the eta and pion `exclurad.F`). So running this file will give results identical to vcut=0 (no cut), not the documented alternate mode \u2014 worth knowing before you interpret the output."
